      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "If you want to make robots, drones (the OC ones, not the GT ones), or tablets, you\u0027ll need one of these. First you need a \u0027template\u0027, which is the case for the device, tablets and drones have their own cases, but robots just use computer cases. From there, you\u0027ll want to pick out what you\u0027d like to put into them.\n\n[warn]Once assembled, components can only be retrieved with a dissassembler, which will lose some items![/warn]\n\nIf you want to have *some* configurability, you can install the upgrade / card container upgrades, although those can use up a lot of complexity.\n\nComplexity is really just an \"OP\" meter used to keep you from having really powerful components in a tiny weak drone, and the maximum is determined by the template item.\n\nFun fact: The assembler will expose itself as a component, letting you start it remotely and check its status!",
